ie morocco global news toronto  [Music]  still ahead billing the billionaires the  push for taxing the world ultra wealthy  luck is not on the side of four  astronauts with the spacex mission they  were supposed to wrap up their six-month  mission on the international space  station and return to earth today first  bad weather has delayed their departure  to monday and get this the capsule  they're coming back on has a broken  toilet so they'll have to wear diapers  for their eight-hour journey home  rough ride the cost to launch just one  of those capsules is roughly 55 million  per seat a paltry sum for spacex's  multi-billionaire owner elon musk but as  the world's wealthiest see their  fortunes expand beyond earth they're  still taxed in the u.s at lower rates  than the average person as jackson  proskow reports there's a growing push  for a special wealth tax in a country  that's produced more billionaires than  any other  there's never been a better time to be a  billionaire in america  the ultra wealthy have seen their  fortunes skyrocket  the collective wealth of the top two  elon musk and jeff bezos has risen by  140 billion dollars so far this year yet  they and other billionaires pay no tax  on those gains everybody in this country  that has been blessed and prospered  should pay a patriotic tax that inequity  can be chalked up to the fact that  assets are not considered income until  they're sold billionaires can pay  themselves a relatively small salary and  simply borrow against their immense  wealth on paper to live large and  largely tax-free you might be able to  borrow money from your local bank  and spend that to live a lavish  lifestyle  and enjoy all that increase in the value  of your stock without ever having to pay  tax on that's why some u.s lawmakers are  floating the idea of a billionaire's tax  one that could pay for trillions of  dollars in planned spending the proposal  would target the 700 richest americans  that's anyone with more than one billion  dollars in assets or who makes at least  100 million dollars in annual income i  don't want to punish anyone's success  i'm a capitalist  i want everyone to be able to if they  want to be a millionaire billionaire to  be able to seek their goal  but all i'm asking is  pay your fair share  tesla's elon musk scoffed at the idea  tweeting eventually they run out of  other people's money and then they come  for you  by some estimates musk would owe 50  billion dollars over five years if the  proposal passed i think what it does  address is what many people feel is a  pretty  important unfairness or inequity in the  system there are of course questions  about whether such a specific tax would  be legal or feasible which has left the  proposal on hold for the moment but as  their fortunes continue to grow  america's richest people will all but  certainly face pressure to pay more to  reflect how much wealth they've amassed  jackson prosko global news washington  up next a chance discovery at a thrift  store returns some long lost canadian  honor  take a look at this dozens of colorful  hot air balloons fill the skies of  turkey's ancient cappadocia region this  morning it's one of the country's most  popular tourist destinations and it's  easy to see why the balloons take off  every morning for tourists to catch the  sunrise and glimpses of the unique  volcanic landscape called fairy chimneys  remembrance day will hold a different  meaning to many canadians as we honor  those who paid the ultimate sacrifice  but for one family in winnipeg that day  will now bring extra special  significance thanks to some diligent  detective work in calgary as gil tucker  reports it's all thanks to a chance  discovery in the back of a thrift store  they get all kinds of things coming into  this goodwill donation center in calgary  books clothes um toys  electronics and then one day this past  summer  jonah henderson comes across something  really special i actually just found the  medals canadian forces on it i'm huge  into history so  i thought  this kind of stuff is pretty important  he turns it over to his managers and the  detective work begins  we found the initials j.t and last name  pearson with  just four letters sask we found an  obituary of a john thomas hearson that  he was born in nottingham england and  then had immigrated over to canada and  had settled in waver and saskatchewan we  tracked down  other names from within that obituary we  came across a grandson i didn't really  know that he had the medals so what a  surprise for kelly hearson in winnipeg  it's absolutely wonderful just an  absolute honor to have them and i am  just so thankful to alberta goodwill for  reaching out for taking the time and  making the effort to find me it was just  fantastic like to know we found a family  member it's a really heartwarming  feeling medal's j.t herson won for his  service in both world wars we will look  after them  have them displayed prominently with the  others that i have i have medals from my  father and also from three uncles we are  pretty blessed and it was their  sacrifices which got us where we are  jonah is also grateful for his family's  service my great grandfather  i actually he fought in world war ii  and  i actually have all of his paperwork  from world war ii and he's glad to have  played a part in getting these medals  back where they belong very very uh  satisfying it's a joyful thing bill  tucker global news  that's a great story and that is global  national for this sunday i'm robin gill  tonight your canada is the sun rising  over bird river in manitoba there are so  many beautiful spots all over canada so  please keep sending your pictures to  viewers at globalnational.com  thanks for watching donna friesen is  back tomorrow have a great night  [Music]
 

